// D1597's CLAUSE-1 FACE, and the worst outcome class this repo grades: `vl check` rc 0,
// the module validates, the program exits 0, and it printed the WRONG VALUE. A `const`
// written inside a top-level block is a start-function local; wasm locals are
// function-scoped while VL's module top level is lexically scoped, so this read of the
// module global `n` — outside the block, after it — was claimed by the block's slot.
//
// The block's binding is never READ, which is what rules out a resolution that only
// misfires on a live use. Adding any import at all made it print 9: the merge mangles
// top-level names per module, so the collision exists only in a single-module program.
// The loud face is `tests/cases/scope/module-global-read-claimed-by-block-binding.vl`.
// Should print 9.
if true { const n = 3 }

const n = 9
print(n)
